ighter","title":"Swamp banshee (variant 3)","variant":""},{"detail":"","key":"creature/q23g%20human%20archer%20f","title":"The Chosen One's archer","variant":""},{"detail":"","key":"creature/q23g%20human%20mage%20f","title":"The Chosen One's sorceress","variant":""},{"detail":"","key":"creature/q23g%20human%20fighter%20m","title":"The Chosen One's warrior","variant":""},{"detail":"","key":"creature/zone15%20human%20citizen%20f","title":"Village woman (variant 2)","variant":""},{"detail":"","key":"creature/zone15%20human%20citizen%20m","title":"Villager (variant 2)","variant":""},{"detail":"","key":"creature/zone15%20human%20fighter2%20m","title":"Warrior (variant 2)","variant":""},{"detail":"","key":"creature/zone15%20toad1","title":"Young poisonous toad (variant 3)","variant":""}],"title":"Creatures and people"},{"id":"quest","rows":[{"detail":"","key":"quest/q23g","title":"The Chosen One's Weapon","variant":""},{"detail":"","key":"quest/q14g","title":"The Weaponsmith","variant":""}],"title":"Quests"},{"id":"exit","rows":[{"detail":"","key":"map/gz10g","title":"Foothills","variant":""},{"detail":"","key":"map/gz13g","title":"Road to the healer","variant":""}],"title":"Connected locations"}],"versions":[{"guide":"","html":"<article><h1>Village and Ruins</h1><p>Named for the remains of ancient buildings, this region is comparatively safe. Straying from the road can still lead a traveller into serious trouble.</p><h2>The Free Hunters and Babur</h2><p>A <a href=\"wiki://character/loozer\">messenger</a> invites the rescuers of the hunters to <a href=\"wiki://character/karh\">Bor the Cunning</a>’s camp. Bor claims neutrality in the war, yet asks them to act against the village’s hunters and caravans. To question <a href=\"wiki://character/smith\">Babur the Tightfist</a> about the Orb, Kir helps bring him out of the village. The letter can go to Babur himself or to the elder, with different explanations for the craftsman’s arrival. Babur then sends Kir to the lizards’ tomb for a supposed magical needle. The expedition supplies lizard hides, and Babur admits that useful armour material was his real interest. For information about the Orb, he redirects the visitors to Estera. [1, 2, 3, 4, 5, 6, 7, 8]</p><h2>Babur’s knife bargain and captivity</h2><p>Airy’s warning about the depleted Orb leads Kir towards the observatory. Babur can open the blocked approach, but first demands the Chosen’s knife, now a sacred relic. While Kir pursues the relic, island orcs raid the hunters’ camp and carry Babur away. They hand him to their ogre neighbours after his dealings with them turn sour. Kir obtains the two keys to the pit, frees the craftsman and escorts him back alive. Babur renounces further trade with the orcs. His rescue also lets Bor put forward a new plan against the settlers. [9, 10, 11, 12, 13, 14, 15]</p><h2>Babur’s rescue and the restored Orb</h2><p>The stolen Orb stands on an island orc pedestal. Kir obtains the bridge gear from their gathering on Council Mountain to reach it. Once Babur is safe and has seen the damaged Orb, he provides the key to the observatory approach. The observatory book lets Estera prescribe washing the Orb in underground spring water. A landslide closes Kir’s former route to Tka-Rik, forcing him through the old tunnel. Before departure, Airy asks Kel to greet the Chosen if they meet him and says she still remembers him. Kel apologises for her earlier jealousy; both women recognise feelings Kir has yet to understand. The repaired Orb shows snow rather than Jigran. Tka-Rik interprets this as Ingos, agrees that Kel can go with Kir, and warns that greater freedom there does not prevent cruel government or make their search for powerful magic safe. [16, 9, 10, 11, 12, 17, 18, 19, 20, 21, 22, 23, 24, 25, 13]</p><h2>Sources</h2><p>Based on the original dialogue, quest journals, event scripts and world descriptions. Source numbers identify the evidence listed below.</p><table data-columns=\"2\"><tr><th>#</th><th>Sources</th></tr><tr><td>1</td><td>Dialogue · <a href=\"wiki://character/loozer\">Brigand</a>, <a href=\"wiki://character/hero\">Kir</a>, <a href=\"wiki://character/merc2\">Kel</a> (briefing brief_120)</td></tr><tr><td>2</td><td>Dialogue · <a href=\"wiki://character/karh\">Bor the Cunning</a>, <a href=\"wiki://character/hero\">Kir</a>, <a href=\"wiki://character/merc2\">Kel</a> (briefing brief_121)</td></tr><tr><td>3</td><td>Dialogue · <a href=\"wiki://character/karh\">Bor the Cunning</a>, <a href=\"wiki://character/hero\">Kir</a>, <a href=\"wiki://character/merc2\">Kel</a> (briefing brief_123)</td></tr><tr><td>4</td><td>Dialogue · <a href=\"wiki://character/hero\">Kir</a>, <a href=\"wiki://character/karh\">Bor the Cunning</a>, <a href=\"wiki://character/merc2\">Kel</a> (briefing brief_124)</td></tr><tr><td>5</td><td>Dialogue · <a href=\"wiki://character/smith\">Babur the Tightfist</a>, <a href=\"wiki://character/karh\">Bor the Cunning</a>, <a href=\"wiki://character/hero\">Kir</a> (briefing brief_126a)</td></tr><tr><td>6</td><td>Dialogue · <a href=\"wiki://character/smith\">Babur the Tightfist</a>, <a href=\"wiki://character/karh\">Bor the Cunning</a>, <a href=\"wiki://character/hero\">Kir</a> (briefing brief_126b)</td></tr><tr><td>7</td><td>Dialogue · <a href=\"wiki://character/hero\">Kir</a>, <a href=\"wiki://character/smith\">Babur the Tightfist</a> (briefing brief_127)</td></tr><tr><td>8</td><td>Dialogue · <a href=\"wiki://character/hero\">Kir</a>, <a href=\"wiki://character/smith\">Babur the Tightfist</a>, <a href=\"wiki://character/merc2\">Kel</a> (briefing brief_128)</td></tr><tr><td>9</td><td>Dialogue · <a href=\"wiki://character/smith\">Babur the Tightfist</a>, <a href=\"wiki://character/hero\">Kir</a> (briefing brief_139)</td></tr><tr><td>10</td><td>Dialogue · <a href=\"wiki://character/karh\">Bor the Cunning</a>, <a href=\"wiki://character/hero\">Kir</a>, <a href=\"wiki://character/merc2\">Kel</a> (briefing brief_140)</td></tr><tr><td>11</td><td>Dialogue · <a